#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""watch-forks-menubar — macOS menu bar widget for live fork counts.

Polls the same ps surfaces as ~/bin/watch-forks (via importlib reuse), shows
the top fork count + total CPU in the menu bar, and renders the top-N
offenders in a custom-view popover dropdown.

Architecture (Phase 2):
    NSStatusItem (from rumps) → NSStatusBarButton click → togglePopover_
    NSPopover (transient) → NSViewController → custom NSStackView layout
        header (NSTextField)     ← _create_header_view / _update_header_view
        separator (NSBox)
        scroll view → row stack  ← _create_row_view / _update_row_view (×N)
        separator (NSBox)
        footer row (Settings ▾, Refresh, Open in Terminal, Quit)

The two _create_*_view / _update_*_view override points are the *whole reason*
this phase exists. Phase 3 will replace _create_row_view with a custom NSView
(icon + name + sparkline + gauge + CPU); Phase 4 will replace _create_header_view
with a multi-sparkline overview. Today both return plain NSTextField views
rendering today's text exactly — visual parity with the NSMenu version.

Persisted settings: interval, top N, sort by are stored in
  ~/Library/Application Support/watch-forks-menubar/settings.json
and reloaded at launch.

Live-updates while the popover is open: NSTimer in NSRunLoopCommonModes (same
pattern as before — strictly speaking NSPopover doesn't suspend the default
run loop the way NSMenu tracking does, but common modes is harmless and
consistent with the rest of the AppKit-driver code).

Launch:  ~/bin/watch-forks-menubar &
Quit:    popover footer → Quit (or pkill -f watch-forks-menubar)
"""
